The bird's eye view version doesn't attempt to insist that everyone
have the same metaphysics; rather, it insists that everyone apply their
metaphysics consistently. If you only know one American and think that
she will go out with you, and you think that there aren't many more
Americans or that you can generalize based on her, then it would be
appropriate for you to claim that lo'e merko would go out with you.
Someone who is more familiar with Americans might point out that your
knowledge about Americans could be improved a bit.

